{"at":"-","bindings":"<path>","event":"opened","ir":"835c3d7e2761aa436515b2e525950569f26b7557567e014a1f7656fab87788ce","prev":null,"protocol":{"description":"Fix the project context, the vision and the roadmap (docs/phases.md steps 4 to 6). Every project context default (audience, source and target language, platform and operating systems, kind of thing, deployment and licence) is recorded as an assumption and checked; the context, the vision and the roadmap are each approved by a person. An approval is a record bound to the revision it decided, approved or rejected, produced only by an action that needs the authority owner.approve, once per revision; after a rejection the artifact's writer is admissible and its new revision is checked and approved again. A revised requirements list invalidates the context check; a revised vision invalidates the roadmap approval. The case ends passed once the roadmap is approved; nothing about epics or specifications happens before that. Late findings (docs/trial-2.md, \"The late-finding loop\"): the context check also runs the consistency rules of the context against the requirements list and reads the open findings, and is not valid while one is open; no vision or roadmap is written or approved then. amend.upstream resolves an open finding by amending the questions and the requirements list, which moves the requirements to a new revision, so the context check is observed again.","id":"sdc.direction","revision":7},"seq":0}
